    "summary": "SOL v1 froze 23 Monte-Carlo predictions a day on Orca Whirlpool bands and published them as cumulative pre-registration manifests: 52 freeze instants, 1,196 predictions, 2026-07-30 .. 2026-09-21. It is retired. Its question (will a fixed band beat a threshold net return?) is superseded by SOL v2, which forecasts a band-breach-margin tier for every tracked pool daily under its own sealed standards. On the public record, v1 ends as follows: one genesis verdict (published, UNTESTED); 12 cohorts that WILL be verdicted under the standing acceptance standard v1 as they mature (2026-09-24T12:17:50Z .. 2026-10-05T12:19:26Z); and 39 cohorts that never had a pre-committed standard and will never receive a verdict.",
